  - Cost: zero; local evaluation                                                                     
   
  5. Timers                                                                                          
  - Signal: wall clock
  - How: setTimeout anchored to state entry or to other events. "Fire on_idle if no speech for 10s," 
  "fire on_session_max if session > 30min"                                                          
  - Commitment point: the timer expires and is still valid (not cancelled by another event)          
  - Used for: idle detection, session caps, per-agent duration limits, retry logic         
  - Cost: zero                                                                                       
                                                                                                     
  6. Observer classifier (Layer 3, opt-in)                                                           
  - Signal: rolling window of recent transcript                                                      
  - How: a cheap parallel model (Haiku, Flash, or a local classifier) sees the last N seconds of     
  transcript and emits structured labels: frustration, escalation, safety, language switch, off-topic
  - Commitment point: when the classifier returns a confidence above a threshold, with a debounce    
